  dialogueText: 'When you want to talk about moving from one place to another, you
    can use the verb ''mapan.''


    It means ''go.''


    For example, if you''re
    heading toward a scenic photo spot, you can say ''mapan.''


    Listen carefully:
    mapan.


    Now, try saying ''mapan'' yourself.'
